==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|ecke}}, from {{inh|de|goh|ecka}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*aggju}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*agjō}}. Compare {{cog|en|edge}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈɛkə/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Ecke.ogg}}
* {{rhymes|de|ɛkə|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f|dim=chen}}

# [[corner]], [[edge]]
#: {{hyponyms|de|q1=seen from the inside|Winkel|Nische}}
#: {{uxa|de|Ich habe mich an der '''Ecke''' vom Tisch gestoßen.|I bumped into the '''corner''' of the table.}}
#: {{uxa|de|Der Tisch steht in der '''Ecke.'''|The table stands in the '''corner.'''}}
# a roughly [[triangular]] or [[quadrangular]] [[piece]] of something
#: {{uxa|de|Gib mir mal eine kleine '''Ecke''' von dem Kuchen.|Give me a small '''piece''' of the cake, please.}}
# {{lb|de|chiefly|colloquial}} [[region]], [[area]], [[neighbourhood]]
#: {{uxa|de|Ihr wohnt ja hier in ’ner ganz netten '''Ecke.'''|You guys live in a nice '''area''' around here.}}
# {{lb|de|colloquial}} [[bit]], [[tad]]
#: {{uxa|de|Es gibt Metal und Death-Metal, das ist dann nochmal ’ne '''Ecke''' härter.|There’s metal and there’s death metal, which is a '''tad''' harder still.}}
# {{lb|de|graph theory}} [[vertex]], [[node]]
#: {{syn|de|Knoten}}
# {{lb|de|ball games|short for {{m|de|Eckball}} or {{m|de|Eckstoß}}}} [[corner]], [[corner kick]]
#: {{syn|de|q1=Switzerland|Corner}}
# {{lb|de|ball games|short for {{m|de|Torecke}}}} one of the two areas of a [[goal]] near where the [[post]] and [[goalline]] meet; {{rfdef|de}}
#: {{coordinate terms|de|q1=area between between post and crossbar|Winkel}}

